            0.114,
            0.026,
            0.841,
            0.046
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 13 — Our Home: Earth, a Unique Life Sustaining Planet"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.897,
            0.039,
            0.932,
            0.052
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "225"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.084,
            0.744,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "biodiversity is key as diverse ecosystems are stronger and more balanced. Local communities can play a big role in using natural resources sustainably."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.141,
            0.744,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Everyone can help. Reusing, repairing, and recycling items like clothes and plastic reduce pollution and waste. Small actions like saving energy and water add up. Learning more, sharing ideas, and encouraging others also makes a difference."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.217,
            0.744,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In conclusion, sustaining life on Earth needs action from all of us—from local communities to global leaders. By working together and living responsibly, we can protect this unique planet and its future."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.322,
            0.27,
            0.343
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.36,
            0.755,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Our Earth is a unique planet in the solar system as it supports life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.38,
            0.757,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Earth orbits the Sun at a distance where the temperature is neither too hot nor too cold, which allows water to exist in liquid form. This region is called the habitable zone or Goldilocks zone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.77,
            0.295,
            0.931,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.77,
                0.295,
                0.931,
                0.423
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.433,
            0.756,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Further, the Earth orbits the Sun in a nearly circular orbit ensuring that the Earth is not too hot or too cold during any part of the year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.469,
            0.755,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Earth’s gravity is just enough to not let atmosphere escape into space. It is also not too high where creatures would be crushed by their own weight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.522,
            0.755,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Presence of ozone in the atmosphere prevents harmful ultraviolet rays from reaching the surface of the Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.559,
            0.755,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The magnetic field of the Earth shields it from high-energy particles that would otherwise hit the Earth and destroy life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.595,
            0.757,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The atmosphere (consisting of air), hydrosphere (consisting of water), geosphere (consisting of the solid part of the Earth), and biosphere (consisting of life) interact and together sustain life on the Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.665,
            0.754,
            0.683
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Reproduction is essential to ensure the continuity of life on Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.684,
            0.587,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reproduction can be either asexual or sexual."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.703,
            0.755,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In asexual reproduction, a single parent produces new individuals that are exact copies of itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.74,
            0.755,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sexual reproduction make it possible for new features to appear in the following generation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.776,
            0.755,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In different animals, the development of the zygote into an embryo takes place either inside or outside the body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.812,
            0.756,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Climate change, biodiversity loss, and pollution are threatening life on Earth. Together, these challenges are known as the triple planetary crisis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
